Incrementally clone Parquet and Iceberg tables to Delta Lake: What is the syntax for clone?: Clone for Parquet and Iceberg uses the same basic syntax used to clone Delta tables, with support for shallow and deep clones. For more information, see Clone types.
Databricks recommends using clone incrementally for most workloads. Clone support for Parquet and Iceberg uses SQL syntax.  


Clone for Parquet and Iceberg has different requirements and guarantees than either clone or convert to Delta. See Requirements and limitations for cloning Parquet and Iceberg tables.
To deep clone a Parquet or Iceberg table using a file path, use the following syntax:
``sql
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE <target-table-name> CLONE parquet./path/to/data`;

CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE  CLONE iceberg./path/to/data;
To shallow clone a Parquet or Iceberg table using a file path, use the following syntax:sql
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE  SHALLOW CLONE parquet./path/to/data;
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE  SHALLOW CLONE iceberg./path/to/data;
You can also create deep or shallow clones for Parquet tables registered to the metastore, as shown in the following examples:sql
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE  CLONE ;
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE  SHALLOW CLONE ;
```

